+/*-------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ *
+ * zou_walredo.c
+ *	  Sandboxed WAL redo worker for the zou page service.
+ *
+ * Started as "postgres --zou-redo <scratchdir>".  The page service keeps a
+ * pool of these workers and materializes page versions by shipping a base
+ * page image plus the chain of WAL records that touch it, then reading the
+ * result back.  The worker runs the real rmgr redo routines against a
+ * purely in-memory smgr, so it needs no data directory contents beyond an
+ * empty scratch directory (used for the sysv shmem interlock key and a
+ * per-process scratch file that feeds the AIO read path).
+ *
+ * Protocol, little endian, on stdin/stdout.  Requests are a tag byte
+ * followed by a u32 payload length and the payload:
+ *
+ *	 'R' len=0
+ *		 Reset.  Drops every page and buffer left over from the previous
+ *		 batch.  Every batch must start with this.
+ *	 'P' spc u32, db u32, rel u32, fork u8, blk u32, page image (BLCKSZ)
+ *		 Push a base page image into the in-memory store.
+ *	 'A' lsn u64, end lsn u64, WAL record bytes (header included,
+ *	     xl_tot_len long); the end lsn is where the next record starts in
+ *	     the real stream, page headers included, since redo routines stamp
+ *	     it into pages as the page LSN
+ *		 Apply one record through its rmgr redo routine.
+ *	 'G' spc u32, db u32, rel u32, fork u8, blk u32
+ *		 Read a page.  Answered with 'O', len u32 = BLCKSZ, page image.
+ *
+ * Any malformed message or redo failure exits the process; the pool
+ * restarts workers on EOF.  WAL records arrive over a trusted local pipe
+ * from the page service, which already CRC-checked them at ingest, so the
+ * worker validates lengths but not record checksums.
+ *
+ * The worker deliberately skips the normal control file, lock file and
+ * catalog machinery: redo routines operate below the relcache and only
+ * need shared memory, the buffer manager and the rmgrs.  A fabricated
+ * in-memory control file (see ZouRedoInstallFakeControlFile in xlog.c)
+ * reports checksums off, so materialized pages carry stale checksums and
+ * the page service must recompute them before serving tenants that have
+ * checksums enabled.
+ *
+ * On Linux the worker installs a seccomp allowlist before touching the
+ * first request, so a compromised redo routine cannot open files, connect
+ * sockets or spawn processes.  Set ZOU_REDO_NO_SANDBOX=1 to skip it for
+ * debugging.  Other platforms run unsandboxed and are for development
+ * only.
+ *
+ * Custom WAL resource managers are not registered here, so records from
+ * extensions with custom rmgrs fail the batch.  Wiring those up is left
+ * until a tenant actually needs it.
+ *
+ *-------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ */
+
